{"title":"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Nicholas is counting the sheep in a flock as they cross a road. The sheep begin to cross the road at 2:00 p.m. and cross at a constant rate of three sheep per minute. After counting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0d6c36fdad9c2874053be46c7e4120f2edcf47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> sheep, Nicholas falls asleep. He wakes up an hour and a half later, at which point exactly half of the total flock has crossed the road since 2:00 p.m. How many sheep are there in the entire flock?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/a/35abe8211c9f35abed38a4833291d10fa1aa0b57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 630 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 621 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 582 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 624 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 618$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"421\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Nicholas sleeps for an hour and a half, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcfee7bd8a5e15e5f6b7881c138de43651572a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minutes.  Since three sheep cross the road per minute, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/1/a011af37322bcaf05a55df004d1b3eda37f3d189.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\times 90 = 270$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> sheep cross while he is asleep.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0d6c36fdad9c2874053be46c7e4120f2edcf47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> sheep crossed before he fell asleep, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/0/52043c548a98f4f2236c3c6c0c625cae07c8bf5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42 + 270 = 312$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" /> sleep have crossed the road in total when he wakes up.\nSince this is half of the total number of sheep in the flock, then the total number in the flock is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/9/ee96da121a6045171ac1fdc9e572713918da9773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 312 = 624$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"100\" height=\"13\" />.  Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problem